          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scott"
            },
            "datePublished": "2022-05-23",
            "reviewBody": "Dr Mehta was assigned to me by mission hospital.  My T-1 had a teardrop break and my c-1 had an arch break.  I told Mehta I was a surfer and to please save my mobility.  He said “I am not concerned with you surfing”.  He fused my c7-t3 twelve degrees forward so my 20lb head was set seriously off balance, he installed excess metal rods that blocked my c6 from moving, he did not put all my muscle fibers or fascia back together and used metal staples not dissolvable stitches which left a terrible scar and separated muscles.  I thought my life was over, never surf again, and I would have serious strain forever. No follow up or care about me by Mehta.  I questioned him as to why and his answers were disheartening.   I found a great surgeon out of UCLA Dr. Lanman who straitened my neck, took the metal out, installed an artificial disk at c5-c6, put my muscle fibers and fascia back together, and smoothly used dissolvable stitches.  All my strain is gone and my neck is straight and balanced.",
